    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1220">

                <pb facs="1324" n="1314" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg1314"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6266A/10: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Representative to the French Committee of
                        National Liberation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Chapin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-21T12:00:00+01:00">February 21,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 7:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>559. With reference to the treatment to be accorded Axis diplomats accredited to
                    the Vatican after the occupation of Rome, the British Foreign Office has
                    recently informed its Ambassador to the Holy See<anchor n="56" xml:id="d1220-f1"
                    /> that any such diplomats found outside the Vatican City when Allied troops
                    entered Rome would have to be given the immediate alternative of entering the
                    Vatican City or leaving Italy under safe conduct. At the same time Foreign
                    Office stated that it saw no reason why any diplomats already residing in the
                    Vatican, least of all Allied diplomats, should move out to make room for Axis at
                    present living in Rome proper.</p>
                <pb facs="1325" n="1315" xml:id="pg1315"/>
                <p>This matter has been discussed informally with AFHQ<anchor n="57"
                        xml:id="d1220-f2"/> and Makins<anchor n="58" xml:id="d1220-f3"/> and it is
                    felt here that it would be preferable that Axis diplomats should be given safe
                    conduct home without the option of entering Vatican City. It would appear that
                    from a technical point of view they would lose diplomatic immunity if
                    [apprehended?] outside the limits of Vatican City.</p>
                <p>The Department’s instructions would be appreciated. Makins is telegraphing
                    Foreign Office in same sense.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
